knowledge-base/decisions/synthetic-tenants.md:195:| ③ ✅ **BUILT 2026-07-22** | Scenario packs as TAPES (`sick-call-surge` — one REAL bridge stimulus per absence, sync-aligned; `irops-day` — cancelled legs, never actuals; `doc-expiry-wave`; `legality-edge` — violator census ×3 bounded by pool) + **the live-pace player `--pace realtime`/`Nx`** (wall-clock-paced syncs + bridge POSTs via `playTapePaced`/`bridgePoster`; pacing changes arrival time, never content) + tape-replay equivalence + **the DEEP-COHERENCE suite: the REAL legality evaluator over the corpus** | **DONE — 23 tests.** The coherence suite closed ②'s gap and earned its keep with FOUR generator findings, all fixed: (1) the monthly-cap check let the pool burn 90h in ~2 weeks → roster collapse (→ pro-rata pacing); (2) the regime judges a TRAILING window at evaluationTime → breaches must sit adjacent to asOf; (3) its rest rule is LONGEST-rest-in-window (`WEEKLY_REST_24H`) → a rest violator must fly daily, not just once short-gapped; (4) ordinary crew tripped the REAL rolling caps (`FTL_7D` 32h / `FTL_30D` 100h, which calendar-month caps miss across boundaries) → rolling caps in the catalog + rostering. End state: **declared REST/FTL violators trip the real evaluator; NO undeclared crew trips a CRITICAL** — "illegal exactly where declared" now holds against the real regime, not just structurally. `LEGS_PER_DUTY` stays structural-only (verified: the RACP fleet projection carries no per-duty legs rule). Perf: `small` 2-month = 77k rows generated in ~1.3s; `full`-tier seeding remains the documented in-VPC job (④). |
