knowledge-base/index.md:357:- [canonical-clocks-are-instants](decisions/canonical-clocks-are-instants.md) — ✅ **BUILT 2026-08-04.** Three canonical entities stored operational clocks as **minutes-from-midnight integers**, each conceding it in its own doc comment (`grdDutyBegMins` is literally the AIMS column). G1 bars day encodings, but the encoding is the real defect: **a minute-of-day is not a time** — no date, no zone, so `30` is both "00:30 today" and "00:30 tomorrow". Now `scheduledDeparture`/`scheduledArrival`/`reportTime`/`groundDutyStart`/`checkInAt` as Instants, decoded at the Sense seam (minutes ≥1440 roll correctly instead of aliasing). **Killed three latent midnight bugs:** the check-in plane's hand-rolled `spillMins` branch, its `getUTCHours()` UTC assumption, and `crewStatusSnapshot`'s tie-break where a 00:30 departure sorted AHEAD of a 23:40 one. Two `minsToInstant` helpers deleted. The 0-means-unset sentinel moved to Sense. Proven by a test the old encoding could not pass (same instant, two source datings, same side of the window)
