knowledge-base/log/2026/09/W39/_archive.md:391:**Symptom (live preprod run 1, `d2a9480`, switch on).** The second delta tick's 2,000-id overlap put 1,885 horizon pairings into the re-read set (> the 500 cap) → `discontinuity` → the one-per-interval full-tick budget was already spent by the cold start → the tick went DEGRADED and processed nothing, which it would have done on every tick; the steady-state feed cost ~53k logical reads/tick. Separately, `full_caught_total{report}` counted all 41 shortages of the cold-start full tick. **Cause.** The overlap was sized in ids, the wrong unit: 2,000 `LOG_CREWLEG` ids ≈ two days of changes. **Amendment (operator sign-off 2026-09-24):** a clock-free 5-minute overlap anchored on the cursor row's own log time (measured ~170 reads/tick vs ~53k), a degraded tick still re-reads open + parked shortages, and `full_caught_total` counts only when a valid cursor existed at the full tick's start. Measurements and the staging-probe caution are on [uncrewed-delta-scan](features/uncrewed-delta-scan.md) §Live validation run 1. Build: increment ④b.
