knowledge-base/log/2026/10/W41/2026-10-05-feed-completion-noc-port-priority-two-seam-rotation-caught.md:5:**Priority-2 budget seam, finished.** `hourKeyOf` moved to `shapeCost.ts` (the tick and the rotation import it) and `createHourlyPriorityBudget({ ..., now })` names the hour bucket from the clock each time a context is asked for, so a consumer that outlives the hour spends on the current hour's counter, the one the tick spends on. The KB states what M2-18's call site must do (one budget over the feed's store with `sourceBudget` as limits, `budgetedRead(budget(2), "getDisruptedFlightLegs", ...)`, no last-run stamp for a cycle that deferred a line). The shape has no `costSeeds` key, so it prices at its rows until measured: a contract key and an operator decision.
knowledge-base/log/2026/10/W41/2026-10-05-feed-retarget-rosteractivity.md:3:**What landed.** `rosterLinkedFeedTick.ts` carries two entities, RosterActivity and ConnectionLeg: a log signal is one scoped read through the producer (`syncRosterActivityForCrews`), an absence-classed signal is read first at priority 1 (and announced to an optional `onAbsenceScopes` hook, the seam M2-20 uses), a refused reservation or a skipped catalogue pass parks the scopes as pending scope items the next tick drains, and `resolveCrewLegAssignmentDaysForLegs` is no longer called. `rosterLinkedCoverageRotation.ts` walks RosterActivity's live window through `syncRosterActivityDay` (coverage keys `{system}:{day}`, frozen days outside the window left alone, the first reads of a cold window held to the next clock hour) and keeps ConnectionLeg's `runWindowSync` path. New `sync/shapeCost.ts`: a call debits `max(ceil(rows × ratio), costSeeds.<shape>)` (6.29 fleet day, 10.1 scoped, 11.25 audit), a timeout debits the seed times `timeoutDebitFactor` and never the cost item (`ReadContext.settleFailure`). The log read gained the overlap: `seen` list in the cursor item, late signals with their age, `codeSignals`, `codeOnly` scopes, unknown-operation rows ignored and counted; C14's durable form drops an absence signal whose log id an emitted or retracted report holds. `sync.json` (six tenants, strict schema): `costSeeds`, `timeoutDebitFactor`, `feed.enabled` moved from CrewCheckIn/CrewLegAssignment to RosterActivity. Deleted: `rosterLinkedRedate.ts`, its timer, `CanonicalFeedRedateFailing`, `canonical_feed_redate_*`, `canonical_feed_items_total`. Added: `SyncFeedItemsStore.countItemsByKind`, `canonical_feed_items{kind}` with per-kind bounds in `CanonicalFeedItemsUnbounded`, `CanonicalFeedLateSignals`. Design and as-built text: [canonical-sync](../../../../features/canonical-sync.md) §2a.18.
