knowledge-base/reference/canonical-data-map.html:409:    <ul><li>A1 never reads vr_FlightMembers: deadhead comes from CREWLEG.PAX on the line's single CREWLEG match; the FM-only lines (P10, P10b) are a daily audit read (A21).</li><li>One output row per ROSTER row key: the CREWLEG match is aggregated per key (several → no pairingRef, never two lines).</li><li>READ COMMITTED with RCSI; no NOLOCK, no FORCE ORDER, no hint forcing a join order through a view.</li><li>Freshness is LOG_ROSTER-driven: a signal on (crew, d) is a scoped re-read of [d − 1, d + 1] anywhere in the window (≈ 18 reads per crew-day).</li><li>The only fleet reads are the coverage rotation's per-day reads (≈ 37k each at the anchor day): over the live window inside the rotation share, and once per history day for the backfill, after which history is frozen (ruling 0.8-1); there is no hourly sweep and no multi-day fleet call.</li><li>Every call is debited against the per-clock-hour budget (S24) at its priority or the history share; a timeout debits the shape's seed × 2 and moves its breaker to half-open (aims_shape_tripped after 3 in a row).</li></ul>
knowledge-base/reference/canonical-data-map.html:412:    <ul><li><b>Live:</b> [today − 3, today + horizon]: the coverage rotation keeps each day fresh (T3); days still open to correction (late CHECK_IN, same-week edits)</li><li><b>History:</b> [today − lookback, today − 4]: backfilled once (after a reset or at go-live), newest day first, then FROZEN (ruling 0.8-1); a LOG_ROSTER signal that touches a frozen day still triggers its scoped re-read</li><li><b>Backfill:</b> ≈ 370 days × 37k ≈ 13.7M logical reads per reset at rows × 6.29 (ruling 0.9-2), in the history share: ≈ 92 hours. The 45-day reach (52 days with the straddle extension) is covered within about 13 hours (newest first). crew_roster_history_reads_per_hour alerts when it is under half the share for 3 h while history is uncovered (lens 2 M3).</li><li><b>Legality:</b> legality's readCoverage gains rosterCoverage (the uncovered fleet days and the crew's own uncovered days in the read window, per system); a metric whose read window holds one is NOT_EVALUATED for that crew. rosterCoverage is threaded into every readCoverage site: domains/airline/crew/legality/src/windows/assemble.ts:219-226 and domains/airline/crew/readplanes/src/fleetLegalitySnapshot.ts:644-646, domains/airline/crew/projection/src/fromCanonical.ts:121-128, domains/airline/crew/recovery/src/compose.ts:175-180 and the scenario delay resolver (domains/airline/crew/scenario/src/canonicalDelayResolver.ts:47, today unbounded); the earliest-ingested rescue and dayAggregates' known_zero rescue (domains/airline/crew/legality/src/windows/dayAggregates.ts:267-275) are suppressed while the window is uncovered, so a backfill frontier is never a first duty. readWindow's maxLookbackDays (domains/airline/crew/legality/src/windows/readWindow.ts:94) is the derived lookback for the annual family (lens 1 NM8, lens 2 M9, M10)</li><li><b>Coverage providers:</b> coverage is kept per (tenant, system), each with its provider: AIMS, the coverage rotation; N-OC, the mirror, whose live days count as covered only while its last completed cycle is younger than T3 (a stalled mirror uncovers them); days before the mirror's history depth are not_applicable; the synthetic seed declares coverage over the whole window relative to its play clock (days outside the tape covered-empty, stated). For legality, not_applicable and no row are uncovered for any metric whose reach crosses them (lens 2 M9)</li><li><b>Covered:</b> ruling 0.10-4. A day is covered for the fleet (per system) when its last read completed. A crew-day is uncovered when the durable ledger holds an unresolved refused, quarantined or subject_pending line of that crew on that day; it uncovers that crew only. readRosterCoverage(window, system) returns the fleet days and the per-crew exceptions; the mapping completeness check runs over every code referenced in the window, obsolete ones included. The fleet day is a UTC LEG_DAY (ruling 0.10-3); a crew-day exception is keyed by the line's dutyDate (base-local); a subject_pending crew (no base, so no dutyDate) is excepted on all its days, and legality maps its base-local read window onto both</li><li><b>Policy changes:</b> a change of the compiled activity mapping re-derives the affected lines in the store (no AIMS read, minutes; the crew-days being re-derived are uncovered for those crews only); a carrier-map change re-derives the carrier refs the same way; a source-calendar change touches no RosterActivity field. No lock change re-reads history from AIMS (lens 2 M6)</li><li><b>Audit:</b> the frozen-day audit lives in the history share after the backfill: day d is audited on the day (epoch(d) mod 30), capped at ⌈lookback / 30⌉ ≈ 13 days a day, so audits never synchronise after a reset; crew_roster_frozen_audit_oldest_age_seconds alerts at 45 days. A changed fingerprint is frozen_day_drift (counter, any increase); only lines inside the read's population are compared (lens 2 M11, lens 1 N-m7)</li><li><b>Cost:</b> Per shape, rows × the shape's measured reads per row until measured IO (⑤-b) merges: the fleet-day A1 read (live rotation, backfill, audit) 6.29 (ruling 0.9-2; tools/canonical-model/evidence/a1-cost-2.out:4), the scoped re-read 10.1 (1,580 reads / 156 rows, tools/canonical-model/evidence/a1-cost-3.out:5), the A21 audit 11.25 (64,023 / 5,692, tools/canonical-model/evidence/a1-cost-1.out:6); every call is floored at its shape's seeded minimum (tenants/&lt;id&gt;/sync.json costSeeds, from the 1-crew-1-day measurement), never at 1 row (domains/airline/crew/adapters/src/sync/rosterLinkedFeedTick.ts:323-325). A wall-time proxy needs no IO capture: aims_call_wall_per_row against the anchor (0.125 ms per row, tools/canonical-model/evidence/a1-cost-2.out:3); above 5× it is aims_cost_proxy_overrun (warning), which pauses the history share until it clears (lens 2 M4). The built settle counts rows (domains/airline/crew/adapters/src/sync/rosterLinkedFeedTick.ts:321), so the multiplier is applied there.</li></ul>
