knowledge-base/reference/rearch/39_racp_legality_master.md:64:- **Time base:** store UTC; convert to a **configurable reference timezone** only to find calendar boundaries (day/month/year). ONE reference clock per tenant/regime, applied to all that tenant's crew. **`referenceTimezone` is RegimeConfig (per tenant) — NOT hardcoded** (user directive Session 9: another airline may run a different TZ). **Copa value = America/Panama (UTC−5, no DST) — CONFIRMED (user, Session 9).** The window-mechanic golden files for the Copa regime use America/Panama; the calculator takes the tz as a parameter so other regimes drop in unchanged.
knowledge-base/reference/rearch/39_racp_legality_master.md:65:- **Four window mechanics** (the highest-correctness-risk detail): (1) rolling clock @ block events; (2) calendar-day, minute-split at midnight; (3) calendar-month sliding, minute-split at month boundary; (4) resetting calendar (FTL-CM only). Boundary attribution: rolling = minute overlap; day/month = split at boundary; FTL-18H = any-overlap leg count.
knowledge-base/reference/rearch/39_racp_legality_master.md:68:- **No acclimatization/TZ-adjustment rule** in this regime (unlike EASA/FAR117) — only the fixed Panama reference clock.
