knowledge-base/reference/rearch/54_c10_provisioning_ask.md:61:## 6. Validation plan (how we prove the replica is adequate BEFORE committing the shadow clock)
knowledge-base/reference/rearch/54_c10_provisioning_ask.md:62:Before any shadow gate clock starts, run a **load rehearsal**: point all readers at the replica at projected peak concurrency, measure (a) replica health headroom (CPU/IO/connections/replication lag), (b) per-reader latency, (c) whether lag stays within the freshness bound under load. This both DE-RISKS the hard-blocker and produces the day-1 numbers the `51` §4 ledger needs (e.g. the `40`/`37` watermark-skew + the `48`/`32` latency budgets). A failed rehearsal triggers the §3 fallback BEFORE we've committed a window.
knowledge-base/reference/rearch/55_reference39_scoping.md:62:`39` is a LIVING doc (v2.0, June 2026; `39` §I.3). When it revises, **production + `reference_39` + the goldens** must update under a controlled protocol so they never silently drift apart (a regulatory analog of the D15 ledger). A `39` revision = a tracked event: re-derive the affected goldens from raw-reg FIRST, then update production AND reference independently, then re-run the differential harness. Pre-register this protocol before the S3 clock starts.
