knowledge-base/reference/replacement-rules-gap-analysis.md:86:| 13 | Special duty / airport-category codes (Vuela de Prueba 33, Carguero 124/132, MEX 70, MEX/NLU 143) | **BUILT (dcortex side + adapter source-read — 2026-06-29, `c77956c`)** | `solver.py` `_special_airport` (cockpit must hold required ATOS categories) + canonical `CrewMember.atosCategories` (dba-reviewed; optional read, optional upsert for writer back-compat, `pii.none` non-neg ints) + prep reads it → `crew_categories` (reserve + llm_proposed; adapter now emits the active-dated CREWCAT codes) | The airport-category gate + the held-category seam are **wired end-to-end** in dcortex. **⚠ "no category column" REFUTED (VPN 2026-06-29):** the crew-category data EXISTS — source = `CREWCATEG` (crew `ID` → `CREWCATIDX`, `ACTIVEBEG`/`ACTIVEEND`) ⋈ `CREWCAT` (`CREWCAT` → `DESC_`); legacy already reads it as `crewCategory: {crewCat, description}`. dcortex's CREWQUAL enrichment ([convert.ts:389](../../domains/airline/crew/adapters/src/aims/convert.ts)) reads `POS/AC/CWBASE` only, NOT the category. **✅ ADAPTER SOURCE-READ DONE (`c77956c`):** `mssqlDb.getCrewCategories()` reads **active-dated** `CREWCATEG` (`ACTIVEBEG <= today <= ACTIVEEND` via `DATEDIFF` on the source clock; ~37.7k of 94.6k active — so EXPIRED airport quals never falsely pass the safety gate) → `crewMembersFromAims` → the reader emits real codes on `CrewMember.atosCategories` (was `[]`). Live-validated (`tools/aims-source-verify.mjs`); 177/177 adapter tests. **Remaining = deployment config only:** set `specialAirportCategories` (airport IATA → CREWCAT code) per tenant. **Caveat RESOLVED (VPN 2026-06-29):** `CREWCAT` is a general 240-row crew-category table whose airport/duty-qual subset IS the ATOS vocabulary — this rule's own example codes ARE CREWCAT codes (`33`=Vuela de Prueba, `70`=MEX/NLU, `124`/`132`=Carguero LNA/CM, `143`=NLU; plus `49`=TGU, `68`=UIO, `69`=GUA, `62`/`76`=US Cat 3A), populated (94,595 CREWCATEG assignments / 9,563 crew; code 70 held by 2,983). The `specialAirportCategories` config maps airport IATA → the CREWCAT code (TGU→49, MEX→70, GUA→69, UIO→68, …). The special **duty** codes (33/124/132) are the **same CREWCAT source** (not separate) — only their *use* (duty-gate vs airport-gate) differs. |
knowledge-base/reference/replacement-rules-gap-analysis.md:104:| 9 | On-station crew | **BUILT — Tier-0 (LAYOVER) populator + pipeline + ordering(config)** | the ON_STATION solver pipeline + `buildProblem` merge + `pipelinesByBucket` (rearch/70) + NOW a real `makeOnStationLayoverPopulator` (cortex-runtime, 2026-06-29) discovering Tier-0 LAYOVER crew from the synced `CrewLegAssignment` (inbound arr=hub + outbound dep=hub spanning the window, FlightLeg-joined clock, config ground/report buffers; pure/deterministic) | Wired STRUCTURAL-INERT (`CR_ONSTATION_ENABLED` default-OFF + `CR_ONSTATION_HUB_IATA`); fires only at the ON_STATION cascade scope. **Tier-1 (deadhead-arrived) BUILT (2026-07-03, dba-approved `CrewLegAssignment.role`):** the board widened from PAX=0 to PAX IN (0,1); `buildCrewLegAssignments` stamps role; the populator discovers Tier-1 DEADHEADING_ARRIVED (deadhead inbound to hub, open-ended presence, ranked below LAYOVER). Consumer audit done (EXTRA_FA + 3 read-planes exclude deadheads). **Tier-2/3 (nearby-transit) BUILT (2026-07-03, dba-approved `NearbyStationPresence` entity, Option 1):** a new canonical entity (one boardable (crew, transit-flight) option — a DISTINCT source population from the hub-only board, since the legacy `crewSwap/nearbyTransit` Step A+B+cross-join is not derivable from `CrewLegAssignment`) + `makeOnStationNearbyTransitPopulator` running the DEMAND-dependent Step C tier split (transitReady = transit STA + 60 vs cutoff = demand STD − 45 ⇒ Tier-2 no-delay / Tier-3 delay / drop; boardability DEPARTS_BEFORE_CREW_ARRIVES enforced here, CREW_LEAVES_BEFORE_TRANSIT via the solver's `_onstation_boardability`), composed with the Tier-0/1 populator into `onStationCandidatesFor` (best-tier-per-crew). Solver UNCHANGED (already modeled `transit_flight_std`/`next_assignment_std`/`NEARBY_TRANSIT`). Wired STRUCTURAL-INERT (`CR_ONSTATION_NEARBY_ENABLED` default-OFF). **The live adapter read (`getNearbyStationPresence`) is LIVE-SMOKED + REWORKED (`b9e56af`, 2026-07-04, `tools/nearby-transit-verify.mjs` vs the AIMS replica).** Two DOMAIN corrections from the user reshaped it: it is for a **NON-BASE shortage station** (not the hub — a base/hub shortage fills from its own reserves), and **BASE feeders are EXCLUDED** (a base feeder has reserves too). This is both correctness AND the perf fix — it bounds the presence scan to small non-base feeders (the whole US network + PTY-fed spokes correctly return 0 in ~2.5s; only rare intra-region spoke↔spoke fires, e.g. SJO←GUA = 86 rows / ~16s). The read is now **DEMAND-DRIVEN**: `syncNearbyStationPresence(watermark, date, targetStations)` builds the board only for the open-shortage non-base stations; `subsidiary.reserveBases` drives the feeder-exclusion + target-skip (config-collapsed from `opts.baseStations`, `cdb1af6`; see [[subsidiary-scoping]]). Live-smoke also FOUND + FIXED a **CRROUTE-per-leg cartesian** (174→139k rows without the `crRouteDesc` one-label-per-route dedup) + RESOLVED the STA-wrap (LEGMAIN.STA is pre-wrapped ⇒ raw `DAY*1440+STA` correct). itest now locks both. The demand-driven sync is WIRED (`2814c5c`): `buildNearbyStationPresenceSyncTask` reads the open CoverageDemands → their flight-leg departure origins (shortage stations) → syncs the board for those non-base targets, in `aimsShadowPoller` behind the opt-in `nearbyTransit` flag (no-op with no demands). Remaining for activation: enable the `nearbyTransit` poller flag + `CR_ONSTATION_NEARBY_ENABLED` + `readerOptions.subsidiary` (`reserveBases` for feeder-exclusion/target-skip; `crewBases` for the crew-pool scope). Perf follow-up: scope the `crewBase`/`crRouteDesc` CTEs to day-window keys if target volume grows. **Subsidiary crew-pool scope (rearch/33, 2026-07, [[subsidiary-scoping]]):** the presence pool is now carrier-scoped (`eae79ef`, the crew's operated inbound-leg carrier, all 3 branches) AND crew-base-scoped (`92160a0`/B.3, `subsidiary.crewBases`, all 3 branches — closes the deadhead residual a P5 crew riding a CM leg in); the `crewBase` CTE is active-dated (`2bf4178`/B.1). **Policy slot SPECIFIED + TEST-LOCKED (2026-06-29):** the confirmed order is `["R","ON_STATION","EXTRA_FA","SA","L"]` (after R / before SA/L — Legacy reconciliation, user 2026-06-28; supersedes the v0.3 doc's "after SA/L"); `cascadeOrder` is deployment config (`CR_SOLVE_CONFIG_PATH`), not repo code, and `dispatch.test.ts` "ON_STATION policy slot" proves the DEFAULT `bucketsForStage` walks that order. |
