tools/canonical-model/inputs/blueprint-0.12.md:1849:- **One version space.** ONE per (system, RosterActivity): the per-entity sync sequence sync-seq:{tenant}:{system}:RosterActivity, the multi-stream feed rule of knowledge-base/features/canonical-sync.md:862-874. The roster log is a SIGNAL, not a writer. Reads in two loops interleave safely: a later read reserves a later version, and the feed's clock-free overlap re-delivers a signal an older read may have raced (knowledge-base/features/canonical-sync.md §2a), pinned by an interleaving test.
tools/canonical-model/inputs/blueprint-0.12.md:4061:- Every call is debited against the per-clock-hour budget (S24) at its priority or the history share; a timeout debits the shape's seed × 2 and moves its breaker to half-open (aims_shape_tripped after 3 in a row).
tools/canonical-model/inputs/blueprint-0.12.md:4077:- **Coverage:** each window day is a durable coverage item of the existing roster-linked coverage rotation (stratum.sync_feed_items). A live day is covered while its last completed fleet read is within T3; a history day is covered once its backfill read completed and stays covered (frozen). After a reset every day is uncovered: live days are served first, at their usual priorities; the history backfill runs in the history share (entities.RosterActivity.historyShare, tenants/<id>/sync.json, 150k reads per hour at Copa), a separate counter: while it runs every priority ceiling is lowered by the share (P1 450k, P2 440k, P3 240k, P4 90k), so the worst hour stays ≤ S11 (600k + 150k is never spent with 2 × the largest call on top, lens 2 M3; lens 2 NB-M1). The rotation starts at the next clock hour after a reset, so a reset never double-spends an hour (lens 2 m9).
tools/canonical-model/inputs/blueprint-0.12.md:4082:- **Coverage providers:** coverage is kept per (tenant, system), each with its provider: AIMS, the coverage rotation; N-OC, the mirror, whose live days count as covered only while its last completed cycle is younger than T3 (a stalled mirror uncovers them); days before the mirror's history depth are not_applicable; the synthetic seed declares coverage over the whole window relative to its play clock (days outside the tape covered-empty, stated). For legality, not_applicable and no row are uncovered for any metric whose reach crosses them (lens 2 M9).
