tools/canonical-model/reviews/0.9/critic-0.9-lens2.md:52:| B3 | The timeout debit wipes the whole hour for every priority, and the fail-closed breaker sits on shapes shared by live work | **BLOCKER** | On a timeout the call is debited "276k reads per second" of wall time (`cet:4042`). At the 30 s default (`mssqlDb.ts:238`) that is 8.28M against a 600k allowance. The settle adds `actual − est` to the one hour counter, and every reserve requires `reads_spent + est <= ceiling` (`cs:493`; P1's ceiling is the allowance, `cs:503-509`). So one timeout of any shape blocks every AIMS read, including the P1 LOG_ROSTER reads that carry sick-call signals, for the rest of the clock hour. That breaches the 300 s critical on `absence_signal_latency` (`cet:4821`). `AIMS_REQUEST_TIMEOUT_MS` is env-overridable; at the probes' 120 s it is 33M. The breaker is "per shape, fail closed until an operator re-arms" (`cet:4834`), and every call can trip it (`cet:3996`). The per-day fleet A1 read serves the live rotation, the backfill and the audit alike (`cet:1821`, `cet:4018`). One transient timeout (the adapter documents ECONNRESET over a high-latency link, `mssqlDb.ts:229-232`) therefore stops live coverage until a human acts. All live legality goes NOT_EVALUATED after T3 (6 h, `tenants/copa/sync.json:6`). A tripped log-read shape stops sick calls. Today the code writes the last actual into the shape's cost item (`rosterLinkedFeedTick.ts:311`). If the debit lands there, the re-armed shape's estimate is 8.28M and it can never reserve again: the NB-M4 wedge, back. | Debit a timeout at most the shape's seeded estimate × k (k from `sync.json`), never a rate × wall bound that exceeds the allowance. Never write a timeout's debit into the cost item. Give the breaker a half-open state: auto-retry after a backoff, trip fail closed only after N consecutive timeouts, and count every trip. Give live rotation, backfill, audit, scoped re-read and log read **distinct** shapes and breakers, and never trip the P1 log read fail closed. Name the re-arm command. Red tests: a single 30 s timeout leaves P1 reservable within the hour; a tripped backfill shape leaves live days covered. |
tools/canonical-model/reviews/0.9/critic-0.9-lens2.md:61:| M9 | Coverage-port semantics are open, and four legality paths bypass it, failing open during every backfill | MAJOR | (1) `not_applicable` days ("before the mirror's own history depth", `cet:4015`) have no legality rule. Treated as covered, a Porter crew's 365-day cap is evaluated on a shallow mirror and under-counts; treated as uncovered, annual is NOT_EVALUATED for ever. (2) The synthetic seed covers "the tape's days" (`cet:4015`), but the tape spans fixed `months` from an anchor (`domains/airline/crew/synthetic/src/generator.ts:63-71`). Most of `[today − 365, today + horizon]` is never covered, so `RosterHistoryIncomplete` (critical) fires for ever on copa-local and copa-dev, and the M2 smoke's "non-zero evaluated-crew count" (`cet:4907`) is at risk. (3) N-OC coverage has no freshness bound: a stalled mirror leaves live days "covered". (4) The rescue suppression and `rosterCoverage` are specified only for `assemble.ts:219-226` and `fleetLegalitySnapshot.ts:644-646` (`cet:4012`). Other sites still feed `crewEarliestIngestedDutyMs`: `projection/src/fromCanonical.ts:121-128` and `recovery/src/compose.ts:175-180`. `legality/src/windows/dayAggregates.ts:267-275` marks every day before the earliest ingested duty `known_zero`, which is the backfill frontier during a backfill. `scenario/src/canonicalDelayResolver.ts:47` reads unbounded (`completeFromMs: null`), so its coverage check is inert (`assemble.ts:221`). (5) A day with no coverage row at all (no provider yet, wrong `system`) has no stated meaning. | Define `not_applicable` for legality as uncovered for any metric whose reach crosses it, and state the provenance. Have the synthetic seed declare coverage over the whole window relative to its play clock (outside the tape: covered-empty, stated). Bound N-OC live coverage by the mirror's last completed cycle (T3). Thread `rosterCoverage` into every `readCoverage` site, including the scenario resolver, and suppress the `dayAggregates.ts` rescue too. Declare "no row = uncovered", with a red test per call site. |
